<title>SOUTH KOREA: Samick trading halted on default talk.</title>
<headline>Samick trading halted on default talk.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading in shares of South Korea's Samick Musical Instruments Co was halted on talk the company had defaulted on promissory notes, the Korea Stock Exchange said.</p>
<p>Trading was halted at 10:05 a.m. (0105 GMT).  </p>
<p>A Samick spokesman confirmed that it missed a 2.7 billion won payment on Tuesday, but said it would pay back the sum by the legal deadline on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Samick's shares last traded at 6,140 won, down 390 from Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
</text>
